{"step_index":94,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-11T14:49:35Z","content":"### Task Settled: **PROVEN** (`prove_8ca1b27c : Candidate`)\n\nThe multi-agent teamwork pipeline has settled the conjecture:\n$$\\text{Candidate}: (\\text{nontrivial } G) \\implies 2 \\le \\text{sub\\_total\\_domination\\_number}(G)$$\nwith a kernel-checked proof in [Challenge_8ca1b27c.lean](file:///mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/handoff/promising13/task_8ca1b27c/Challenge_8ca1b27c.lean).\n\n---\n\n### Key Mathematical Idea\n\n1. **Degree bound on simple graphs**: For any simple graph on $n$ vertices without self-loops, the neighborhood of every vertex $v$ satisfies $N(v) \\subseteq V \\setminus \\{v\\}$, so $\\deg(v) \\le n - 1 < n$ ([`SimpleGraph.degree_lt_card_verts`](file:///mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/handoff/promising13/task_8ca1b27c/reference/GraphInvariantsComputable.lean)).\n2. **Sub-total domination definition**:\n   $$\\text{subTotalDominationNumber}(G) = \\min_{t \\le n} \\{ t \\mid n \\le \\text{largestDegreeSum}(G, t) \\}$$\n   with fallback to $n$ if no prefix reaches $n$.\n3. **Prefix evaluation for $t < 2$**:\n   - At $t = 0$: the degree sum over $\\emptyset$ is $0 < n$ (since $n \\ge 2$).\n   - At $t = 1$: the sum over any singleton $\\{v\\}$ is $\\deg(v) < n$.\n4. **Conclusion**: Since no $t \\in \\{0, 1\\}$ satisfies $n \\le \\text{largestDegreeSum}(G, t)$, the minimal satisfying index (or the fallback $n$) must be $\\ge 2$.\n\n---\n\n### Checker Output\n\n```text\nLINT: ok\n/tmp/tmp.KBwzJ5HmCn.lean:65:8: warning: declaration uses `sorry`\n'prove_8ca1b27c' depends on axioms: [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound]\n'refute_8ca1b27c' depends on axioms: [propext, sorryAx, Classical.choice, Quot.sound]\nCHECK: elaborated. Allowed axioms: propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound.\n       'sorryAx' in a list above means that theorem is unfinished.\n```\n\n- **Exit code**: `0`\n- **Axioms used for `prove_8ca1b27c`**: Standard Lean axioms only (`propext`, `Classical.choice`, `Quot.sound`).\n- **Audit**: Independent 3-phase Victory Audit confirmed compliance with all integrity and verification rules.\n\nFull details are documented in [REPORT.md](file:///mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/handoff/promising13/task_8ca1b27c/REPORT.md)."}
